From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vlad Panazan <git@praznet.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 16:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] host: avoid libc++ logging from JVM_Exit

Hosted APKs can load their own libc++_shared.so. Its symbols may interpose on
the host libc++ used by android-base, making a late LOG stream unsafe. Grayjay
calls Runtime.exit from its uncaught-exception handler and reliably crashed in
std::__put_character_sequence before ART could invoke the exit hook.

Keep the informational message, but write it through the C stdio ABI so
JVM_Exit reaches CallExitHook and FastExit even after an APK loads libc++.
---
 openjdkjvm/OpenjdkJvm.cc | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/openjdkjvm/OpenjdkJvm.cc b/openjdkjvm/OpenjdkJvm.cc
index c0f874f..e113063 100644
--- a/openjdkjvm/OpenjdkJvm.cc
+++ b/openjdkjvm/OpenjdkJvm.cc
@@ -340,7 +340,10 @@ JNIEXPORT void JVM_GC(void) {
 }
 
 JNIEXPORT __attribute__((noreturn)) void JVM_Exit(jint status) {
-  LOG(INFO) << "System.exit called, status: " << status;
+  // App-bundled libc++_shared libraries can interpose on the host libc++ used by
+  // android-base logging. Do not enter a C++ iostream while terminating a hosted
+  // application; that can crash before the ART exit hook gets a chance to run.
+  fprintf(stderr, "I/artopenjdk: System.exit called, status: %d\n", status);
   art::Runtime::Current()->CallExitHook(status);
   // Unsafe to call exit() while threads may still be running. They would race
   // with static destructors.
-- 
